<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <!-- The shared coding-agent harness: launching and supervising processes in a checkout, and
         rendering, spawning and reading back a coding-agent session on top of that.

         IT EXISTS BECAUSE THERE WERE TWO COPIES. `qits-commands` and `qits-coding-agents` lived
         inside qits-projects-daemon and inside qits-workspace-daemon, under two package roots, and
         they had drifted: one copy grew AgentDesk and its tickets steering, the other grew the
         plugin service, prompt refinement and three MCP servers where the first attaches one. Every
         harness change had to be written twice or land on one side only, which is how the drift
         happened and how it would keep happening. The union of both copies is what moved here, and
         both daemons now depend on this artifact instead of carrying a copy.

         TWO MODULES, NOT ONE, because `qits-coding-agents` does not compile without
         `qits-commands` — Command, CommandService, CommandRegistry, ChatProtocol, ForeignPty — and
         `qits-commands` was duplicated in exactly the same way. Leaving it behind would have made
         one library depend on two different daemons' copies of the other; publishing both
         de-duplicates the same problem twice.

         FRAMEWORK-FREE, both modules: no Quarkus, no CDI, no JAX-RS, no Jackson, no configuration
         reading. That constraint is what lets a Quarkus daemon and a plain-JVM daemon both embed
         it, it is what lets it link into a GraalVM native image with nothing to register, and it is
         why steering prompts are Java text blocks a unit test asserts byte for byte rather than
         classpath resources. The one framework dependency is vertx-core, and only for
         io.vertx.core.json.

         WHAT THE HOST DAEMON SUPPLIES, rather than this library knowing it: the ambient identity of
         the checkout (CheckoutContext), the scope-to-MCP-server mapping with its narrowing and its
         pre-approval lists (AgentMcpServers), where the MCP servers are (McpEndpoints), the
         instance defaults (AgentDefaults), and the action table (ActionResolver). Everything else
         is here.

         VERSIONS ARE CalVer, STAMPED AT RELEASE. Every pom carries the version verbatim rather than
         deriving it, the same way qits-registries-javalib does, so the release stamp rewrites one
         literal per pom and `deploy` at the root publishes both modules together. The daemons pin a
         released coordinate, so a shared harness change is release-library-then-bump-daemons — see
         README.md.

         THE REACTOR ROOT IS `qits-agents`, NOT `qits-coding-agents`: the published module keeps the
         artifactId the daemons already import, and a parent cannot share an artifactId with its own
         module. `qits-agents` is the component directory this repository sits under in the wrapper,
         which is the honest name for "both of these together". groupId is `eu.wohlben.qits`, as
         every other published javalib on this platform uses — the daemons' in-repo copies sat under
         plain `eu.wohlben` because they were modules of a daemon rather than artifacts anyone
         resolved. -->
    <groupId>eu.wohlben.qits</groupId>
    <artifactId>qits-agents</artifactId>
    <version>2026.913.151200</version>
    <packaging>pom</packaging>
    <name>qits-agents</name>

    <modules>
        <!-- Dependency order: the agent module launches its sessions as commands, never the other
             way round. -->
        <module>qits-commands</module>
        <module>qits-coding-agents</module>
    </modules>

    <properties>
        <maven.compiler.release>25</maven.compiler.release>
        <project.build.sourceEncoding>UTF-8</project.build.sourceEncoding>
        <project.reporting.outputEncoding>UTF-8</project.reporting.outputEncoding>

        <!-- PINNED, NOT IMPORTED FROM THE QUARKUS BOM. Both daemons managed these two through
             quarkus-bom, because both daemons are Quarkus applications and had the import anyway.
             Here there is no Quarkus: importing a ~400k-line platform BOM to learn two version
             numbers would be the only Quarkus fact in a repository whose whole point is not having
             one, and it would silently move both libraries whenever the platform moved. The values
             are what quarkus-bom 3.34.6 managed at the move, so the moved suites run against
             exactly what they ran against in the daemons. -->
        <vertx.version>4.5.26</vertx.version>
        <junit.version>6.0.3</junit.version>

        <compiler-plugin.version>3.15.0</compiler-plugin.version>
        <surefire-plugin.version>3.5.4</surefire-plugin.version>

        <!-- REPRODUCIBLE BUILDS. Without this, maven-jar-plugin stamps each jar's manifest and
             zip entries with the wall-clock time of the build, so two builds of the SAME commit and
             SAME version produce different bytes. That is not a hypothetical: a release of this
             repository can fail partway — qits-commands-2026.913.151200.jar deployed, then the SBOM
             step failed on an unrelated platform gap — and a retry re-runs `mvn deploy` against the
             same tag and the same version. The store accepts a re-upload of identical bytes, so a
             retry needs the second build to be byte-identical to the first, and only the timestamp
             stood in the way. The value below is fixed and arbitrary — CalVer already makes every
             released version distinct, so this property only has to be the SAME on every build of
             one commit, not meaningful on its own. maven-jar-plugin honours it from 3.2 on; this
             reactor's effective version (3.4.1) already does. -->
        <project.build.outputTimestamp>2026-09-13T00:00:00Z</project.build.outputTimestamp>
    </properties>

    <dependencyManagement>
        <dependencies>
            <dependency>
                <groupId>io.vertx</groupId>
                <artifactId>vertx-core</artifactId>
                <version>${vertx.version}</version>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <groupId>org.junit.jupiter</groupId>
                <artifactId>junit-jupiter</artifactId>
                <version>${junit.version}</version>
                <scope>test</scope>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <!-- The reactor's own module, so the agent module depends on it version-less and
                     moves at the reactor's version. -->
                <groupId>${project.groupId}</groupId>
                <artifactId>qits-commands</artifactId>
                <version>${project.version}</version>
            </dependency>
        </dependencies>
    </dependencyManagement>

    <build>
        <pluginManagement>
            <plugins>
                <plugin>
                    <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>
                    <version>${compiler-plugin.version}</version>
                    <configuration>
                        <parameters>true</parameters>
                    </configuration>
                </plugin>
                <plugin>
                    <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
                    <version>${surefire-plugin.version}</version>
                    <configuration>
                        <!-- ForeignPty opens a PTY through java.lang.foreign downcalls, and every
                             spawn in either module goes through it. Without this the JVM warns on
                             every run and, per the warning's own text, will refuse it outright in a
                             future release. Set here rather than per module because both modules
                             spawn. -->
                        <argLine>--enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED</argLine>
                    </configuration>
                </plugin>
            </plugins>
        </pluginManagement>
    </build>
</project>
